/* The single source of truth for libcuda_fake's exported CUDA driver surface.
 *
 * Every row is one EXPORTED SYMBOL (one entry point in the .so). It drives,
 * in this order:
 *   1. the TF_SYM_* index enum used by the per-symbol call counters,
 *   2. the tf::kSymbols[] table used by cuGetProcAddress / cuGetProcAddress_v2,
 *   3. the control-API enumeration (tf_symbol_name_at and friends),
 *   4. the linker version script (generated by CMake from this file), so the
 *      .so cannot export a cu* symbol that is not in this table.
 *
 * TF_ROW(exported, base, version, stream_kind)
 *
 *   exported     the exported symbol name, e.g. cuMemAlloc_v2. Must name a
 *                function defined in entry_points.cc.
 *   base         the name an application passes to cuGetProcAddress, e.g.
 *                cuMemAlloc. Several rows share a base; cuGetProcAddress picks
 *                between them by version and stream kind.
 *   version      the CUDA version in which THIS entry point was introduced,
 *                encoded as 1000*major + 10*minor. These are not invented:
 *                each one is read from the PFN_<base>_v<version> typedef that
 *                CUDA 12.6's cudaTypedefs.h declares for that entry point.
 *   stream_kind  TF_STREAM_NONE          the entry point takes no stream, or
 *                                        has no per-thread-default variant;
 *                TF_STREAM_LEGACY        a NULL stream argument means the
 *                                        context's legacy default stream;
 *                TF_STREAM_PER_THREAD    a NULL stream argument means the
 *                                        calling thread's per-thread default
 *                                        stream (the _ptsz / _ptds entries).
 *
 * This file is #included several times with TF_ROW defined differently; it has
 * no include guard on purpose.
 */

